Focus on macro-economic indicators like inflation, unemployment and GDP growth. Only consider news sources from large reputable news outlets like The Wall Street Journal, and the Financial Times. Weight indicators where positive announcements such as decreasing inflation and strong GDP growth will greatly increase sentiment scores. Assume that policy makers will follow best practices when these indicators point in healthy directions. Weight your conviction score with the consistency across multiple, independent, reputable news sources. If the S&P500 is already trending upward compared to the Monday opening, increase both sentiment and conviction slightly.